  "question": {
    "text": "There is a stream of neutrons with a kinetic energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0327</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>. If the half-life of the neutron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn></math> second, what fraction of neutrons will decay before they travel a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>? Given the mass of neutron = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>675</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>.",
